{"id": "86118", "name": "AlgMap-3.1", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<p>Express the following, as a single fraction: \\[{{CT:0}}+{{CT:1}}.\\] <br /> [[input:ans]] <br /> <br /> Leave your answer in it's lowest terms in the form \\(\\frac{a}{b}\\). [[validation:ans]]</p>", "generalfeedback": "<p>In this case the denominators of the fractions are equal so you simply add the numerators to obtain the numerator and the denominator stays the same.</p>\n<p>The general rule is: \\[\\frac{a}{b} + \\frac{c}{b} = \\frac{a+c}{b} \\] In this exmaple: \\[{{CT:0}}+{{CT:1}} = \\frac{{{CT:2}}+{{CT:3}}}{{CT:4}} = {{CT:5}}.\\]</p>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": false, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "EqualComAss", "sans": "ans", "tans": "ta", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "1-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans", "tans": "(a+c)/(b+d)", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-1-T (naive adding of fractions)", "feedback": "<p>Remember that the first step in adding fractions is to make both denominators equal. It is not simply adding the numerators and the denominators.</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-1-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 2, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans", "tans": "ta", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-2-T ", "feedback": "<p>Simplify the fraction fully into the form \\(\\frac{a}{b}\\) and leave in it's lowest terms.</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "1-2-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["a", "b", "c", "d", "lcm", "ta"], "nvariants": 5}